    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* --- The Fubini–Study metric on ℂP¹, from one scalar function --- */\n/* Treat z and z̄ as independent symbols, which is the standard device for\n   computing ∂∂̄ without splitting into real and imaginary parts. */\nKpot : log(1 + zz*zb)$\ngzzb : ratsimp( diff( diff(Kpot, zz), zb) )$\nprint(\"Kähler potential K = log(1 + |z|²)\")$\nprint(\"   g_{zz̄} = ∂²K/∂z∂z̄ = \", gzzb, \"   = 1/(1+|z|²)²\")$\nprint(\"   ONE real function determines the whole metric.  Compare Stage 4,\")$\nprint(\"   where a metric in real dimension 2 needs 3 independent\")$\nprint(\"   components and in dimension 4 needs 10.\")$\n\n/* the same thing in real coordinates */\ndeclare([xv, yv], real)$\nrr2 : xv^2 + yv^2$\nconf : 1/(1 + rr2)^2$                  /* ds² = conf·(dx² + dy²) */\ngFS : matrix([conf, 0],[0, conf])$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"in real coordinates z = x + iy :  ds² = \", conf, \" (dx² + dy²)\")$\n\n/* Gaussian curvature of a conformal metric e^{2φ}(dx²+dy²) is −e^{−2φ}Δφ */\nphi : ratsimp( log(sqrt(conf)) )$\nlap : ratsimp( diff(phi, xv, 2) + diff(phi, yv, 2) )$\nKconf : ratsimp( -lap/conf )$\nprint(\"   writing ds² = e^{2φ}(dx²+dy²) with φ = \", phi)$\nprint(\"   Δφ = \", lap)$\nprint(\"   K = −e^{−2φ}Δφ = \", Kconf)$\n\n/* cross-check with the Stage 4 machinery */\nts(e) := ratsimp(trigsimp(e))$\nchristoffel_hand(g, vars) := block([ginv, n_],\n  n_ : length(vars),  ginv : ratsimp(invert(g)),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( sum( ginv[k][l]*( diff(g[j][l], vars[i]) + diff(g[i][l], vars[j])\n                        - diff(g[i][j], vars[l]) ), l, 1, n_)/2 ),\n    j,1,n_), i,1,n_), k,1,n_) )$\nriem_hand(g, vars) := block([G, n_],\n  G : christoffel_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( diff(G[l][j][k], vars[i]) - diff(G[l][i][k], vars[j])\n        + sum( G[l][i][m]*G[m][j][k] - G[l][j][m]*G[m][i][k], m, 1, n_) ),\n    k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_), l,1,n_) )$\nriem_low_hand(g, vars) := block([Rr, n_],\n  Rr : riem_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( sum( g[l][m]*Rr[m][i][j][k], m,1,n_) ),\n    l,1,n_), k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_) )$\nK2d(g, vars) := block([Rm], Rm : riem_low_hand(g, vars),\n  ts( Rm[1][2][2][1] / determinant(g) ) )$\nprint(\"   cross-check with the 4.04 machinery: K = \", K2d(gFS, [xv, yv]))$\nprint(\"   Constant curvature 4 ⟹ a round sphere of radius 1/2, since\")$\nprint(\"   K = 1/R².\")$\n\n/* --- and it IS the round sphere: stereographic projection --- */\n/* Inverse stereographic projection of the UNIT sphere from the north pole. */\nsph : [ 2*xv/(1+rr2), 2*yv/(1+rr2), (rr2-1)/(rr2+1) ]$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"STEREOGRAPHIC PROJECTION (2.05).  The inverse map to the unit sphere:\")$\nprint(\"   σ(x,y) = \", sph)$\nprint(\"   on the sphere ? |σ|² − 1 = \",\n      ratsimp( sph[1]^2 + sph[2]^2 + sph[3]^2 - 1 ))$\nsu : map(lambda([e], diff(e, xv)), sph)$\nsv : map(lambda([e], diff(e, yv)), sph)$\ndt3(a,b) := a[1]*b[1] + a[2]*b[2] + a[3]*b[3]$\nEE : ratsimp(dt3(su,su))$  FF : ratsimp(dt3(su,sv))$  GG : ratsimp(dt3(sv,sv))$\nprint(\"   induced first fundamental form (3.03):\")$\nprint(\"      E = \", EE, \"     F = \", FF, \"     G = \", GG)$\nprint(\"   i.e. ds² = \", EE, \" (dx² + dy²) — conformal, as 2.05 required.\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   That is 4× the Fubini–Study metric, so FS is the sphere of\")$\nprint(\"   radius 1/2:  4·conf − E = \", ratsimp( 4*conf - EE ))$\nprint(\"   Stereographic projection and the Kähler potential log(1+|z|²)\")$\nprint(\"   are the same construction, arrived at from opposite directions —\")$\nprint(\"   2.05 from circle geometry, this from complex analysis.\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Kähler potential K = log(1 + |z|²)\n   g_{zz̄} = ∂²K/∂z∂z̄ =  1/(zb^2*zz^2+2*zb*zz+1)    = 1/(1+|z|²)²\n   ONE real function determines the whole metric.  Compare Stage 4,\n   where a metric in real dimension 2 needs 3 independent\n   components and in dimension 4 needs 10.\nin real coordinates z = x + iy :  ds² =  1/(yv^2+xv^2+1)^2  (dx² + dy²)\n   writing ds² = e^{2φ}(dx²+dy²) with φ =  -log(yv^2+xv^2+1)\n   Δφ =  -(4/(yv^4+(2*xv^2+2)*yv^2+xv^4+2*xv^2+1))\n   K = −e^{−2φ}Δφ =  4\n   cross-check with the 4.04 machinery: K =  4\n   Constant curvature 4 ⟹ a round sphere of radius 1/2, since\n   K = 1/R².\nSTEREOGRAPHIC PROJECTION (2.05).  The inverse map to the unit sphere:\n   σ(x,y) =\n            [(2*xv)/(yv^2+xv^2+1),(2*yv)/(yv^2+xv^2+1),\n             (yv^2+xv^2-1)/(yv^2+xv^2+1)]\n   on the sphere ? |σ|² − 1 =  0\n   induced first fundamental form (3.03):\n      E =  4/(yv^4+(2*xv^2+2)*yv^2+xv^4+2*xv^2+1)      F =  0      G =\n          4/(yv^4+(2*xv^2+2)*yv^2+xv^4+2*xv^2+1)\n   i.e. ds² =  4/(yv^4+(2*xv^2+2)*yv^2+xv^4+2*xv^2+1)\n               (dx² + dy²) — conformal, as 2.05 required.\n   That is 4× the Fubini–Study metric, so FS is the sphere of\n   radius 1/2:  4·conf − E =  0\n   Stereographic projection and the Kähler potential log(1+|z|²)\n   are the same construction, arrived at from opposite directions —\n   2.05 from circle geometry, this from complex analysis."
          ]
        }
      ]
