    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* --- The Kähler condition, and what the area computes --- */\nprint(\"THE KÄHLER CONDITION dω = 0.\")$\nprint(\"   Here ω = \", conf, \" dx ∧ dy, a 2-form on a 2-dimensional space.\")$\nprint(\"   There are no 3-forms in 2 dimensions, so dω = 0 automatically:\")$\nprint(\"   EVERY Hermitian metric on a Riemann surface is Kähler.  The\")$\nprint(\"   condition only starts to bite in complex dimension 2 and above.\")$\n\n/* area of ℂP¹ in the Fubini–Study metric */\nassume(rho > 0)$\narea : 2*%pi * integrate( rho/(1+rho^2)^2, rho, 0, inf )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"AREA.  ∫∫ dx dy/(1+x²+y²)² in polar coordinates:\")$\nprint(\"   2π ∫₀^∞ ρ dρ/(1+ρ²)² = \", area)$\nprint(\"   A sphere of radius 1/2 has area 4πR² = \", 4*%pi*(1/2)^2, \"  ✓\")$\nprint(\"   (The plane covers the sphere minus one point, which has measure\")$\nprint(\"   zero, so the integral is the whole area.)\")$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"GAUSS–BONNET (3.08, 5.06):\")$\nprint(\"   ∫K dA / 2π = \", ratsimp( 4*area/(2*%pi) ), \" = χ(S²) ✓\")$\nprint(\"   K = 4 everywhere and the area is π; the product is forced to be\")$\nprint(\"   4π by topology, whatever the geometry.\")$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"AND THE CHERN CLASS.  5.06 found that a U(1) bundle over S² has\")$\nprint(\"∫F/2π = n ∈ ℤ, with n = 1 the Hopf bundle.  Here\")$\nprint(\"   ∫ω/π = \", ratsimp(area/%pi), \"\")$\nprint(\"   so ω/π is the generator of H²(ℂP¹;ℤ), which is c₁ of the\")$\nprint(\"   hyperplane bundle — the n = 1 monopole of 5.06, met again as a\")$\nprint(\"   Kähler form.  The symplectic form and the curvature of a line\")$\nprint(\"   bundle are the same 2-form.\")$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"BEYOND COMPLEX DIMENSION 1.\")$\nprint(\"   Kähler ⟹ symplectic, and Kähler ⟹ complex, but neither converse\")$\nprint(\"   holds.  The Kodaira–Thurston manifold is compact symplectic and\")$\nprint(\"   admits no Kähler metric at all: its first Betti number is odd,\")$\nprint(\"   and Hodge theory forces b₁ to be EVEN on a compact Kähler\")$\nprint(\"   manifold.  A purely topological obstruction to a geometric\")$\nprint(\"   structure — the same flavour of argument as 4.07's Gauss–Bonnet\")$\nprint(\"   constraint on which surfaces admit which curvature.\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   ℂPⁿ with the Fubini–Study metric is Kähler for every n, is\")$\nprint(\"   SU(n+1)/S(U(n)×U(1)) as 5.03 computed, and is a symmetric space\")$\nprint(\"   of rank 1 in the sense of 5.04 — so it sits at the intersection\")$\nprint(\"   of every thread in Stage 5.\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
